Backport of upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp#32164 (merged 2026-11-14), adapted:
the LFM2 tool-call grammar admits calls to tools that were not declared,
listed last so a declared tool still wins when both parse. Before, a model
that called an undeclared tool was forced onto a declared one or failed to
parse (upstream reports tau3 telecom pass^1 0.746 -> 0.877 on the 24B).
Adaptation for xllama: undeclared calls are allowed only in auto mode.
REQUIRED, and xllama's named tool_choice that maps to it with the named
schema alone, keeps a grammar of declared names only, so a required or
named request still returns a call to a tool it offered (OpenAI semantics,
docs/api-endpoint.md). Upstream enables it for every choice. The
python_style_tool_calls hunk is re-applied by hand: the pin names its rules
"tool-" + name, upstream "tool-" + index. Drop at the #522 pin bump, after
checking upstream's REQUIRED behaviour (xllama #610).

diff --git a/common/chat-peg-parser.cpp b/common/chat-peg-parser.cpp
--- a/common/chat-peg-parser.cpp
+++ b/common/chat-peg-parser.cpp
@@ -559,7 +559,8 @@ common_peg_parser common_chat_peg_builder::python_or_json_value() {
 common_peg_parser common_chat_peg_builder::python_style_tool_calls(
     const ordered_json & tools,
     bool                 parallel_tool_calls,
-    bool                 allow_json_literals) {
+    bool                 allow_json_literals,
+    bool                 allow_undeclared) {
     if (!tools.is_array() || tools.empty()) {
         return eps();
     }
@@ -616,6 +617,18 @@ common_peg_parser common_chat_peg_builder::python_style_tool_calls(
         tool_choices |= rule("tool-" + name, tool_parser);
     }
 
+    // last, so declared tools win when parsing
+    if (allow_undeclared) {
+        auto ident = rule("tool-undeclared-ident", chars("[a-zA-Z_]", 1, 1) + chars("[a-zA-Z0-9_.]", 0, -1));
+        auto value = tool_arg_value(allow_json_literals ? python_or_json_value() : python_value());
+        auto arg   = tool_arg(tool_arg_open(tool_arg_name(ident) + literal("=")) + value + tool_arg_close(eps()));
+        auto args  = optional(arg + zero_or_more("," + space() + arg));
+
+        tool_choices |= rule("tool-undeclared", tool(tool_open(tool_name(ident) + literal("(")) +
+            space() + tool_args(args) + space() + tool_close(literal(")"))
+        ));
+    }
+
     if (parallel_tool_calls) {
         return "[" + space() + tool_choices + zero_or_more("," + space() + tool_choices) + space() + "]";
     }
diff --git a/common/chat-peg-parser.h b/common/chat-peg-parser.h
